# Salmon with Blackened Seasoning

{ rating="5" image="salmon_with_blackened_seasoning.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 1 lb [Salmon]{ ing="salmon" } (or Chicken)
- [ ] 1 tsp [smoked paprika]{ ing="smoked-paprika" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [garlic powder]{ ing="garlic-powder" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [onion powder]{ ing="onion-powder" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [dried thyme]{ ing="dried-thyme" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [Kosher Salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }
- [ ] [Neutral oil]{ ing="neutral-oil" } or butter for blackening

## Recipe

1. Heat a Cast Iron pan on medium heat
1. Season the fish, then sear face down for 8 min. Flip and cook for another 10-15 until done
1. Cook [salmon]{ ing="salmon" } until internal temperature is between 130F (medium-rare) to [145F](https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/safe-temperature-chart) ([wayback](https://web.archive.org/web/20250509133329/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/safe-temperature-chart))
